title: Microsoft Hyper-V VM: Integration services
agents: windows
catalog: os/virtual
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the integration services of a virtual machine running on
 Microsoft Hyper-V. It shows whether each service is enabled.

 By default the check is {WARN} if a service is not active. Only the service
 "Guest Service Interface" is expected to be inactive, and it is always {OK}.
 The expected status and the state are configured with the rule
 "Hyper-V VM integration services", for all services and for single services.
 The VSS service is matched by the name "VSS (Volume Shadow Copy Service)".
 A service with a status other than active or inactive is {UNKNOWN}.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V". The plug-in sends the data
 as piggyback data to a host with the name of the VM.

discovery:
 One service is created on the piggyback host of each VM that reports
 integration services.
